- "Did he give a doll a name?"
+ "Ele deu nome a uma boneca?"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#44 (mes)
- "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
+ "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#45 (mes)
- "Sometimes so much work goes into a doll as if it were their child to doll makers. Kimi was the one for him."
+ "Às vezes se põe tanto trabalho numa boneca que, para o fabricante, ela é como uma filha. A Kimi era isso para ele."
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#46 (mes)
- "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
+ "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#47 (mes)
- "I guess his earnestness breathed life to Kimi."
+ "Acho que a dedicação dele soprou vida na Kimi."
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#48 (select)
- "Do you mean the doll is alive?"
+ "Você está dizendo que a boneca está viva?"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#49 (mes)
- "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
+ "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#50 (mes)
- "Yes, ^0000ffShe^000000 became a living creature. I don't know how, but she is striding in the toy factory with heavy sorrow and rage."
+ "Sim, ^0000ffEla^000000 virou uma criatura viva. Não sei como, mas ela caminha pela fábrica de brinquedos com uma tristeza e uma raiva pesadas."
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#51 (mes)
- "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
+ "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#52 (mes)
- "When I first saw her, she was standing beside the doll maker who died and collapsed. She stood there with a bare expression."
+ "Quando eu a vi pela primeira vez, ela estava de pé ao lado do fabricante de bonecas, que tinha morrido e caído. Ela ficou ali, com o rosto vazio."
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#53 (mes)
- "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
+ "[Catherine Jet Johnson]"
#: npc/re/instances/HorrorToyFactory.txt#54 (mes)
- "That's the end. I was outside when I woke up again after I had blacked out. My face has become like this."
